# LumiBob Log File Schema

## Naming Convention

```
logs/BobsBrain_<YYYY-MM-DD>_<HH-MM>_<6-char-id>_<type>.<ext>
```

Each backtest run produces a set of files sharing the same `<6-char-id>`. Group files by that ID to work with a single run.

**Example run ID `pMLhKf`:**
```
BobsBrain_2026-03-05_15-19_pMLhKf_settings.json
BobsBrain_2026-03-05_15-19_pMLhKf_stats.csv
BobsBrain_2026-03-05_15-19_pMLhKf_trade_events.csv
BobsBrain_2026-03-05_15-19_pMLhKf_trades.csv
BobsBrain_2026-03-05_15-19_pMLhKf_indicators.csv
```

Always prefer `.csv` over `.parquet` — parquet is binary and cannot be read directly.

## File Reference

### `_settings.json`
Key fields: `backtesting_start`, `backtesting_end`, `budget`, `parameters.ticker_limit`, `benchmark_asset` (always `"SPY"`), `backtest_time_seconds`

### `_stats.csv`
Portfolio timeline — one row per event (market open, strategy iteration, market close).

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| `datetime` | Timestamp of the event |
| `portfolio_value` | Total portfolio value at that point |
| `cash` | Uninvested cash |
| `positions` | JSON list of open positions |
| `return` | Cumulative return (decimal) since start |

### `_trade_events.csv`
Full order lifecycle. Each order has multiple rows: `new` (submitted) → `fill` (executed). **Filter to `status=fill` for completed trades.**

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| `time` | Execution timestamp |
| `symbol` | Ticker traded |
| `side` | `buy` or `sell` |
| `status` | `new`, `fill`, etc. |
| `price` | Fill price |
| `filled_quantity` | Shares filled |
| `trade_cost` | Total cost of the trade |
| `trade_slippage` | Slippage incurred |

### `_indicators.csv`
Custom strategy signals. Currently empty (no indicators are being logged by `BobsBrain.py`). Columns: `datetime, name, plot_name, type, value, symbol`.
